# perq station.env fixture — appended to the emitted station.env.
# Three Rivers PERQ-1A running POS G.7 in PERQemu 0.9.5 (github.com/skeezicsb/
# PERQemu, GPLv3), host-native: a stock C#/Mono/SDL2 application under a
# pinned Xvfb, captured with SH_CAPTURE=x11 and driven over XTEST. Not the
# fleet QEMU/MAME — there is no QMP, no save state; the "golden" is the disk
# image plus the boot script, and reset = cold relaunch (docs/lab/PERQ-WAVE.md).
#
# CONTAINED (2026-09-09 host-application rule, same shape as lisa/medley):
# PERQemu AND its Xvfb run inside a systemd-nspawn container — own PID/mount/
# net/IPC/UTS/user namespaces, root inside = host uid PERQ_UID_BASE, the
# release tree bound read-only at /opt/perqemu, work/ the only writable bind
# (perq-inner.sh COPIES the release tree there — symlinking it broke
# MemoryController's ROM opens, see the wave doc's wall 2), capabilities
# dropped, mount syscalls filtered. The host sees the display through a
# symlink /tmp/.X11-unix/X98 -> PERQ_X11_SOCKDIR/X98. mame.pid is PERQemu's
# HOST pid (the idle freezer and the reap-by-exe path); nspawn.pid is the
# supervisor.

# --- PERQemu -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Release v0.9.5 (perqemu0.95.zip, 44605339 bytes, sha256
# 0df4f0c481712741a15ddde48fa3e5fa2eab134d78771bc17969b70c082460de), staged
# by scripts/build-guests/tiles/perq.sh into assets/perq/perqemu.
PERQ_ASSETS=/data/vms/streamhost/assets/perq
PERQ_DISK=g7.prqm
PERQ_BOOTCHAR=
PERQ_GEOM=768x1048
# --- container (systemd-nspawn) ----------------------------------------------
# rootfs: debootstrap minbase trixie + mono-runtime-sgen + libsdl2-2.0-0 +
# libsdl2-image-2.0-0 + xvfb + the audit tools, built and uid-shifted ONCE by
# tiles/perq.sh --rootfs; PERQ_UID_BASE must be a multiple of 65536, distinct
# per station (perq 2359296, accent 2424832).
PERQ_ROOTFS=/data/vms/streamhost/assets/perq/rootfs
PERQ_UID_BASE=2359296
PERQ_X11_SOCKDIR=/run/streamhost/x11/perq
# PERQemu idles at ~200% of a core with nothing happening (§Cost in the wave
# doc) — the standby freeze is mandatory, never run this station unattended.
PERQ_STANDBY_DELAY_S=120

# --- input: XTEST absolute (the Kriz tablet follows the host pointer 1:1) ----
# Wired per the wave doc; NOT yet proven with a two-target readback (POS's
# login shell has no cursor to aim at) — that is why listing.state is hidden.
SH_X11TEST_MOTION=xtest
SH_X11TEST_ABS=1
SH_X11TEST_BUTTONS=xtest
SH_X11TEST_KEYS=1
# Keyboard PROVEN: XTEST type --delay 80 on :98, drop-free, 4/4 chars typing
# `guest`. Not measured below 80 ms — keep the hold/gap conservative.
SH_BTN_MIN_HOLD_MS=150
SH_KEY_MIN_HOLD_MS=80
SH_KEY_MIN_GAP_MS=80

# --- reset / standby ----------------------------------------------------------
# Relaunch only: PERQemu 0.9.5 has no save/restore. Cold boot to the login
# prompt ~20 s, shell ~45 s (measured on the rig, docs/lab/PERQ-WAVE.md).
SH_RESET_MODE=relaunch
SH_FIXTURE_DESC=Three Rivers PERQ-1A (16K CPU, 2 MB, CIO+OIO with Link/Ether/Tape, 768x1024 portrait display, Kriz tablet, 14-inch Shugart) running POS G.7 in PERQemu 0.9.5, host-native under a pinned 768x1048 Xvfb inside a systemd-nspawn sandbox (the bottom 24 lines of the root stay black — PERQemu's own window-sizing margin). At rest: the POS shell, status line "sys:User>Guest>  POS G.7  a-boot" with the clock running and a bare ">" prompt, reached by pressing Return at the date prompt then logging in as `guest` with an empty password. Pointer is ABSOLUTE (Kriz tablet, 1:1 host mapping) but unproven on this character console.

# --- standby -------------------------------------------------------------
SH_IDLE_PAUSE_SECS=60
SH_IDLE_PAUSE_PIDFILE=/data/vms/streamhost/stations/perq/mame.pid
SH_IDLE_PAUSE_PROC_MATCH=/work/perq/PERQemu.exe
SH_IDLE_PAUSE_WARMUP_SECS=180
